  "worked_solution": "If $G=P\\,\\text{i}+Q\\,\\text{j}+R\\,\\text{k}$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $G$ all exist, then the divergence of $G$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n\u2207\\cdot G=\\text{div}\\,G=\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y}+\\frac{\u2202R}{\u2202z}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207\\cdot G & =\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202x}+\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202y}+\\frac{\u2202R}{\u2202z} \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(0)+\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(0)+\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z}(-xy-2{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =-4z.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
